## What the new arms prove (`test/workbench-view.test.ts`, 17/17 pass)

- exactly ONE `conversation.view` registration, `id: "mpd-workbench"`, `label() === "Workbench"`,
  `locale: "mpdWorkbench"`, NO `order`, NO keyed `key`;
- the zh/en tables are key-complete and both render ("MPD 工作台", "2 名成员", "暂停");
- the header carries team id / phase / member count / live hold; the board carries id / owner /
  rendered state; the Pause/Resume pair follows the hold;
- the empty state is explicit in all three shapes (nothing at all, a staged plan, workspace siblings);
- a payload WITHOUT `ok:true` renders "The team routes could not be read." + `HTTP 200`, and is NOT
  rendered as "No team in this session.";
- Pause POSTs `{teamId, reason:"workbench"}` to the hold route, disables BOTH buttons synchronously
  mid-flight (busy label "Pausing…"), then re-reads; Resume POSTs `{teamId}` to the resume route;
- 403 → "The host refused the request (403) …" with the board still rendered and Pause usable again;
  405 → "The route rejected the method (405) …";
- `sessionId` prop → every read carries `?sessionId=`; absent prop → NO `sessionId` is invented;
- a ctx without `slots.inject` → `apply()` does not throw and emits exactly ONE diagnostic line;
- a host that never declares the slot → ONE settle line, `never declared "conversation.view" within 10ms`.

## Bounds (not proven here)

- No browser/DOM run: the registration is proven against the offline harness + the shipped bytes, not
  against a live `dsh web` page. Tab POSITION (registration order) is therefore unobserved.
- The two POSTs are proven against canned responses, not against the parallel lane's server routes
  (`packages/mpd-team-watchdog-plugin/src/web.ts`, present but uncommitted in this tree).
- `VENDOR_LOCK.json` is stale for `client.js` on purpose; `verify:vendor` stays RED until the captain
  re-pins.
